I've never really tried the protection run, so I'm not really familier
with it, but I don't think Wizards are really suited for it.  Low level
wizards are just crappy; no HP, so can't do squat in melee, and for the
first couple levels no PP, so can't do squat with spells.  Heck, at XPL
1, they can get off 1 force bolt, and then it's running time until you
regen a point or two, so you can get off another force bolt, and then
run some more.  So the first few XP levels are MUST HAVE for Wizards.  I
generally try to have XPLv > DLv, down to at least DLv 5.  Sure, don't
over-do the leveling, so that protection won't be too expensive, but I'd
recommend at least get up to XPLv 4 or 5 before cutting back.

