This sounds like a bad-luck bones file.  Giant mimics hit hard, and you
have to get into melee range to even find them.  All I can say, is
barring bones files, you shouldn't meet large or giant mimics until
you've leveled up enough to be able to take them.  Another reason I'd
say the first few XPLvs are a must for Wizards: you have to have enough
HP to take that first hit from the mimic.  Once you've found them,
mimics aren't scary any more (heck, with the right timing [hit, hit,
run; hit, hit, run...], even a Wizard can take them out in melee,
although I would prefer range), but that first hit can hurt a LOT.

> Mimics are a real problem when I'll try not to level up, but I still
> need to go to stores to get money for protection. I'll usually try
> maneuvering around them if my pet doesn't kill them, which is usually
> the case. Doesn't my pet see mimic?
> 

They see what you see.  If you've searched and found the mimic, they
should see it.  If you haven't found the mimic yet, I don't think they
see it.  Note that the Giant Mimic from the bones file might be higher
level than your pet, so your pet wouldn't even try to attack it.

