Early wish for SDSM makes Wizards MUCH easier to survive with.  In fact,
as I think about I'm pretty sure most, maybe even all of the games I
ended up getting down to the Quest, I had SDSM from an early wish.  Of
course, every game that I've gotten past the quest, I've died to
cockatrice corpse.....  But even if you don't get SDSM, I'd still say
stick w/ non-spell interfering armor.  Spells are a Wizard's strength, a
high level Wizard with a nice spell repertoire is very powerful in any
situation, but until you work up your spell repertoire & have lots of PP
for casting, a Wizard is a wimp.  Limiting spell-casting by wearing
metal armor just makes it worse.  And armor doesn't matter unless you
get into melee, and a wizard wants to stay out of melee as much as possible.

> I've tried writing E-word into dust, but many times monsters seem to
> ignore it. One hit is often too much when your HP is 15 and AC 7...
> Engraving E-word takes too long, and I don't always have hard ring or
> gem to write with. Anyways I would prefer not to use Elbereth too much.
> 
